然后另一个人写信来说，我的办公室实际上每隔一个周五放假，我们以前把工作的那周五叫做阿洛哈周五，

653
00:26:15.280 --> 00:26:17.300
and many people wore Hawaiian shirts.
而且很多人穿夏威夷衬衫。

654
00:26:17.740 --> 00:26:22.480
That was early 2000s, and over time, many of the Hawaiian shirt wearers retired.
那是2000年代初，随着时间的推移，许多穿夏威夷衬衫的人退休了。

655
00:26:23.060 --> 00:26:32.380
I recently brought back a few Aloha shirts and started wearing them on Fridays, and one of the old-timers said, damn, I forgot all about Aloha Friday.
我最近翻出了几件阿洛哈衬衫，开始在周五穿，其中一个老员工说，天哪，我都把阿洛哈周五忘得精光了。

656
00:26:32.380 --> 00:26:41.480
A much younger co-worker asked what that was, so we explained that in the old days, many people would wear Hawaiian slash Aloha shirts on Fridays.
一个年轻得多的同事问那是什么，于是我们解释说，在过去，很多人会在周五穿夏威夷或阿洛哈衬衫。

657
00:26:41.840 --> 00:26:46.500
She asked if we could do that again, and we both said, of course, just wear an Aloha shirt.
她问我们能不能再这样穿，我们俩都说，当然可以，只要穿一件阿洛哈衬衫就行。

658
00:26:47.100 --> 00:26:49.320
And, lady, this made me think of our crew.
而且，女士，这让我想起了咱们的团队。

659
00:26:49.580 --> 00:26:52.920
Remember, our crew on Fridays would often wear a Hawaiian shirt.
记住，我们团队在周五经常会穿夏威夷衬衫。

660
00:26:53.080 --> 00:26:53.540
They would.
他们会的。

661
00:26:53.980 --> 00:26:54.300
Yeah.
是啊。

662
00:26:54.440 --> 00:26:56.560
But now we're the old-timers.
但现在我们成了老员工了。

663
00:26:56.800 --> 00:26:57.660
We are.
确实是。

664
00:26:57.900 --> 00:26:59.880
That's like an old-fashioned tradition.
这就像一个老式传统。

665
00:27:00.240 --> 00:27:01.000
I know.
我知道。

666
00:27:01.000 --> 00:27:04.260
And then this fellow from Germany wrote in with this curveball.
然后有个来自德国的家伙抛出了这样一个出其不意的问题。

667
00:27:04.560 --> 00:27:08.760
He said in the thread, does your office have a non-casual Fridays?
他在帖子中说，你们办公室有非休闲星期五吗？

668
00:27:09.280 --> 00:27:11.560
This really got people chatting, okay?
这真的让大家聊开了，好吧？

669
00:27:11.960 --> 00:27:21.440
He said he works in IT, and since his department usually just wears jeans and T-shirts, a group of them thought it would be fun to introduce a non-casual Friday as a bit of a joke,
他说他在IT部门工作，由于他们的部门通常只穿牛仔裤和T恤，他们的一群人觉得作为一种玩笑，引入一个非休闲星期五会很有趣，

670
00:27:21.440 --> 00:27:24.860
where people actually dress up and often kind of formally.
大家会盛装打扮，而且通常穿得比较正式。

671
00:27:26.020 --> 00:27:27.800
And folks love this.
人们非常喜欢这样。

672
00:27:27.940 --> 00:27:34.440
Lady, people shared that they do fancy Fridays or, quote, formal Fridays, or they'll have, like, Thai Thursdays.
女士，大家分享说他们会过精致星期五，或者引用他们的话叫正式星期五，或者他们会有像泰式星期四这样的活动。

673
00:27:34.700 --> 00:27:35.960
Isn't that so funny?
是不是很有趣？

674
00:27:35.960 --> 00:27:36.720
Yeah.
是啊。

675
00:27:37.040 --> 00:27:37.440
Yeah.
对。

676
00:27:37.440 --> 00:27:41.260
It's so crazy because the pandemic really changed office fashion.
太疯狂了，因为疫情真的改变了办公室的时尚。

677
00:27:41.440 --> 00:27:49.720
When everybody was working from home and then it was time to go back into a shared workspace, I think people were like, I'll come back to the office,
当每个人都在家办公，然后又到了重返共享办公空间的时候，我想大家当时的想法是，我会回办公室的，

678
00:27:49.720 --> 00:27:52.160
but I'm not wearing that shit anymore.
但我再也不穿那破衣服了。

679
00:27:52.460 --> 00:27:52.740
Yeah.
是啊。

680
00:27:52.740 --> 00:27:55.080
Like, I want my comfy clothes all the time.
就像，我随时都想穿着舒服的衣服。

681
00:27:55.440 --> 00:27:56.420
I've noticed.
我注意到了。

682
00:27:56.780 --> 00:27:57.080
Yeah.
对。

683
00:27:57.080 --> 00:27:58.500
So now it's, like, flipped.
所以现在情况反过来了。

684
00:27:58.680 --> 00:28:03.800
It's, like, you're casual all week, and then if you want for fun, some people dress up on Fridays.
就像你一整周都很休闲，然后如果你想找点乐子，有些人会在周五盛装打扮。

685
00:28:04.140 --> 00:28:04.460
Yeah.
是啊。

686
00:28:04.600 --> 00:28:06.500
I wonder how long that's going to laSt.
我不知道这能持续多久。

687
00:28:06.500 --> 00:28:19.220
I feel like as newer generations who didn't experience the pandemic start going into the workplace, I wonder if it will become the way it was, if it will become, like, you'll have,
我觉得随着没有经历过疫情的新一代开始进入职场，我不知道它是否会回到以前的样子，是否会变成，

688
00:28:19.220 --> 00:28:22.060
like, this, like, fancier business attire again.
比如，这种更讲究的商务正装再次出现。

689
00:28:22.400 --> 00:28:22.820
Yeah.
对。

690
00:28:22.820 --> 00:28:23.720
I don't know.
我不知道。

691
00:28:23.720 --> 00:28:32.660
Oh, okay, and then two more things that I thought were interesting is one person said they worked at an engineering firm in Texas, and they did a completely optional,
哦，对了，还有两件我觉得很有意思的事，一个人说他在德克萨斯州的一家工程公司工作，他们举办了一个完全自愿但真的很有趣的，

692
00:28:32.660 --> 00:28:40.620
but it was really fun, Western Wednesday, and you could wear cowboy shirts, boots, cowboy hats, and I thought that was kind of fun.
西部星期三，你可以穿牛仔衬衫、靴子、牛仔帽，我觉得这挺有意思的。

693
00:28:40.840 --> 00:28:45.020
Like, I wonder if there are regional dress-up days at different offices, you know?
就像，我不知道不同办公室里是不是也有地区性的盛装日？

694
00:28:45.020 --> 00:28:45.260
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

695
00:28:45.700 --> 00:28:54.940
And lastly, a bunch of folks shared that Friday is a work-from-home day, and most of their colleagues aren't even in the office, and I thought, oh, man,
最后，许多人分享说周五是居家办公日，他们的大多数同事甚至都不在办公室，我想，天哪，

696
00:28:55.180 --> 00:28:56.380
Michael would have hated that.
迈克尔肯定会讨厌那样的。

697
00:28:58.160 --> 00:29:00.480
That's the most casual version of a Friday.
那是周五最休闲的版本了。

698
00:29:00.740 --> 00:29:01.400
It is.
确实是。

699
00:29:01.580 --> 00:29:02.320
So there you go.
所以就是这样。

700
00:29:02.320 --> 00:29:05.120
Those are some casual Friday trends happening now.
这些就是现在正在发生的一些休闲星期五潮流。

701
00:29:05.440 --> 00:29:06.320
Thank you, Angela.
谢谢你，安吉拉。

702
00:29:06.320 --> 00:29:10.860
Well, I want to share a new scene that was added back to the superfan version.
嗯，我想分享一个加长版里加回来 的新场景。

703
00:29:11.380 --> 00:29:16.880
It happens at the Jim-Pam-Dwight desk clump, and Jim has a gift for Pam.
它发生在吉姆、帕姆和德怀特的办公桌区，吉姆给帕姆准备了一份礼物。

704
00:29:17.080 --> 00:29:18.760
He's welcoming her back.
他在欢迎她回来。

705
00:29:18.980 --> 00:29:19.320
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

706
00:29:19.360 --> 00:29:22.800
And she opens it, and it looks homemade.
她打开了，看起来像是手工做的。

707
00:29:23.400 --> 00:29:26.980
It's this little island, and there are little dolls.
这是一个小岛，上面有几个小玩偶。

708
00:29:27.300 --> 00:29:32.080
There's a doll representing her, one representing Jim, one representing Dwight.
有一个代表她的玩偶，一个代表吉姆，一个代表德怀特。

709
00:29:32.620 --> 00:29:33.740
Why don't we listen?
我们为什么不听听看呢？

710
00:29:35.000 --> 00:29:35.960
All right, you ready to wait?
好了，准备好迎接惊喜了吗？

711
00:29:36.840 --> 00:29:37.560
Ready for what?
准备什么？

712
00:29:40.160 --> 00:29:40.940
What's this?
这是什么？

713
00:29:41.260 --> 00:29:42.020
Just a little gift.
只是一小件礼物。

714
00:29:44.640 --> 00:29:49.320
On behalf of desk area clump number one, we welcome you to our little island.
代表第一办公区，我们欢迎你来到我们的小岛。

715
00:29:49.660 --> 00:29:51.140
Love, Jim, and Dwight.
爱你的，吉姆和德怀特。

716
00:29:51.420 --> 00:29:52.800
Okay, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.
好吧，哇，哇，哇，哇，哇。

717
00:29:52.920 --> 00:29:55.120
I had nothing to do with that, okay?
这事我可没参与，好吗？

718
00:29:55.520 --> 00:29:57.960
I miss the storage containers that used to occupy that spot.
我怀念以前占着那个位置的储物盒。

719
00:29:58.160 --> 00:29:59.000
Thank you, Dwight.
谢谢你，德怀特。

720
00:29:59.180 --> 00:30:00.640
And you obscure my view of the shredder.
而且你挡住了我对碎纸机的视线。

721
00:30:00.720 --> 00:30:01.940
Okay, let's get back to the ceremony.
好了，我们言归正传。

722
00:30:02.020 --> 00:30:02.360
Here we go.
开始吧。

723
00:30:03.240 --> 00:30:04.880
Oh, I love it.
哦，我太喜欢了。

724
00:30:05.020 --> 00:30:06.240
That is so cute.
这太可爱了。

725
00:30:06.240 --> 00:30:08.300
It's us and Dwight.
是我们和德怀特。

726
00:30:08.620 --> 00:30:09.880
I'm supposed to be fishing?
我这是在钓鱼吗？

727
00:30:11.400 --> 00:30:11.840
Barbaric.
野蛮。

728
00:30:12.140 --> 00:30:13.140
You're a train conductor?
你是个列车长？

729
00:30:13.380 --> 00:30:14.360
Yeah, that's my job on the island.
对啊，这就是我在岛上的工作。

730
00:30:14.600 --> 00:30:16.040
And I'm a giant Amazon woman.
而我是一个巨大的亚马逊女战士。

731
00:30:16.220 --> 00:30:18.700
We need an attraction to raise money to get the train to the island.
我们需要一个景点来筹钱把火车运到岛上。

732
00:30:18.860 --> 00:30:19.120
It's awesome.
太棒了。

733
00:30:19.520 --> 00:30:21.500
That island is completely implausible.
那个岛完全不合逻辑。

734
00:30:23.770 --> 00:30:24.550
I love it.
我喜欢。

735
00:30:25.370 --> 00:30:26.570
So there you have it.
事情就是这样。

736
00:30:26.710 --> 00:30:28.290
I guess Jim made her...
我猜是吉姆给她做的……

737
00:30:28.750 --> 00:30:29.910
When did he make it?
他是什么时候做的？

738
00:30:29.990 --> 00:30:31.870
How did he make it without her seeing it?
他是怎么在不被她发现的情况下做出来的？

739
00:30:32.410 --> 00:30:34.070
Where does Jim do any of it?
吉姆到底是在哪儿做这些事的？

740
00:30:34.310 --> 00:30:36.010
Like, where do his pranks happen?
比如说，他的恶作剧都是在哪儿发生的？

741
00:30:36.610 --> 00:30:37.290
All of it.
全都是。

742
00:30:37.490 --> 00:30:42.310
I do love, though, that Dwight finds the size of the island disproportionate.
不过我确实觉得好笑的是，德怀特竟然觉得岛的大小不成比例。

743
00:30:42.470 --> 00:30:44.130
Like, this is a guy that loves bobbleheads.
拜托，这可是个喜欢摇头娃娃的人。

744
00:30:44.310 --> 00:30:45.010
You know what I mean?
你知道我的意思吧？

745
00:30:45.430 --> 00:30:45.650
Yeah.
对啊。

746
00:30:46.050 --> 00:30:47.930
Well, don't you wish you still had that prop?
难道你不想留着那个道具吗？

747
00:30:48.430 --> 00:30:50.890
Oh, I would love to have that on my desk right now.
哦，我现在好想把它摆在我的桌上。

748
00:30:51.030 --> 00:30:51.490
I know.
我知道。

749
00:30:51.730 --> 00:30:54.470
Well, thanks to Michael B., again from Lebanon, Pennsylvania.
嗯，再次感谢来自宾夕法尼亚州黎巴嫩的迈克尔·B。

750
00:30:54.530 --> 00:30:57.570
We have this little piece of information about that gift from Jim.
我们得到了关于吉姆送的那份礼物的这一小段信息。

751
00:30:58.110 --> 00:31:02.590
Michael says, according to the Dunder Mifflin accounting actuals that he has from the
迈克尔说，根据他从

