I pronounced it Boss Coves.
我把它发音成了Boss Coves。

776
00:32:10.090 --> 00:32:11.210
And guess what, lady?
你猜怎么着，女士？

777
00:32:11.410 --> 00:32:13.390
That is not how you say it.
根本不是那样念的。

778
00:32:13.650 --> 00:32:14.030
Oh.
噢。

779
00:32:14.030 --> 00:32:17.050
So we got a little fan mail flurry about it.
所以我们收到了不少关于这事的粉丝来信。

780
00:32:17.230 --> 00:32:21.090
And by the way, everyone that wrote in, you guys were really kind with me.
顺便说一句，所有写信的人，你们对我都非常好。

781
00:32:21.250 --> 00:32:21.970
So thank you.
所以谢谢你们。

782
00:32:22.390 --> 00:32:26.170
But I did feel the need to say it properly for you all.
但我确实觉得有必要为大家好好纠正一下发音。

783
00:32:26.550 --> 00:32:30.610
So I'm just going to let the CEO of the company do it so I don't mess it up.
所以我打算让这家公司的首席执行官来念，免得我又读错。

784
00:32:30.790 --> 00:32:33.510
Here's a little snippet of him talking about his store.
这是他谈论自己店铺的一小段音频。

785
00:32:35.670 --> 00:32:38.110
So what the heck is a Boss Coves anyway?
那么，Boss Coves到底是个啥？

786
00:32:38.390 --> 00:32:43.350
Well, we're the largest family-owned department store with 50 stores in this part of the country.
嗯，我们是该地区最大的家族式百货公司，拥有五十家分店。

787
00:32:43.770 --> 00:32:45.630
In Monroe County, you're going to be number 51.
在门罗县，你们将成为第五十一家。

788
00:32:45.730 --> 00:32:47.110
I can't wait to meet you.
我迫不及待想见到你们了。

789
00:32:47.390 --> 00:32:47.850
Come on in.
快进来吧。

790
00:32:47.910 --> 00:32:49.710
Let me show you what a Boss Coves is all about.
让我带你们看看Boss Coves究竟有什么特别之处。

791
00:32:50.910 --> 00:32:51.310
Oh.
噢。

792
00:32:51.870 --> 00:32:52.650
Boss Coves.
Boss Coves。

793
00:32:52.830 --> 00:32:54.190
That was Jim Boss Coves.
那是吉姆·Boss Coves。

794
00:32:54.430 --> 00:32:56.470
Jim, I'm really sorry I got your store name wrong.
吉姆，我真的很抱歉把你的店名念错了。

795
00:32:56.670 --> 00:32:58.150
And the store looks awesome.
而且这家店看起来太棒了。

796
00:32:58.350 --> 00:33:01.890
I mean, that video, I was like, wow, the store has everything.
我是说，看了那个视频，我觉得，哇，这家店应有尽有。

797
00:33:02.350 --> 00:33:04.010
Well, lady, you know what I found out?
好了，女士，你知道我发现了什么吗？

798
00:33:04.010 --> 00:33:06.510
Quote, it almost wasn't Boss Coves.
引述一下，“差一点就不是Boss Coves了”。

799
00:33:06.710 --> 00:33:10.850
In the table draft of this episode, Pam says they got their outfits at, quote,
在本集的剧本围读初稿中，帕姆说她们的衣服是在，引述一下，

800
00:33:11.030 --> 00:33:13.610
Express for Women at the Steamtown Mall.
斯蒂姆敦购物中心的Express女性服饰店买的。

801
00:33:13.790 --> 00:33:16.250
Oh, well, I'm glad they went with the local store, aren't you?
哦，好吧，我很高兴他们选了本地的商店，你不觉得吗？

802
00:33:16.490 --> 00:33:17.650
Yeah, that was a good rewrite.
对，那段重写得很棒。

803
00:33:18.050 --> 00:33:18.330
All right.
好啦。

804
00:33:18.450 --> 00:33:22.470
So now Phyllis has her famous line, close your mouth, sweetie, you look like a trout.
所以现在菲利斯有了她那句名言：“闭上嘴，亲爱的，你看起来像条鳟鱼。”

805
00:33:22.730 --> 00:33:23.110
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

806
00:33:23.670 --> 00:33:28.690
I remember Phyllis told us that that is one of the lines people quote to her most often from the show.
我记得菲利斯告诉过我们，这是观众在剧中引用得最多的一句台词。

807
00:33:29.070 --> 00:33:32.430
Yes, and I've said that it was very hard not to laugh in this moment
是的，而且我曾经说过，在这场戏里要忍住不笑真的很难，

808
00:33:32.430 --> 00:33:38.890
because just any time that sweet, sweet Phyllis has to say something like really biting, it is so funny.
因为每当那个甜美、温柔的菲利斯不得不说出那么刻薄的话时，都太搞笑了。

809
00:33:39.630 --> 00:33:46.790
I also wanted to point out that in the Superfan episode, there is a new top and bottom to the scene that has an extra little joke.
我还想指出的是，在超级粉丝版中，这个场景的前后多出了一个小笑话。

810
00:33:46.950 --> 00:33:49.870
At the top of the scene, Pam is alone in the kitchen.
在场景开始时，帕姆一个人在茶水间里。

811
00:33:49.910 --> 00:33:55.090
She's making her tea, and Creed walks in the door just as the microwave is beeping.
她正在泡茶，而克里德正好在微波炉响的时候走了进来。

812
00:33:55.730 --> 00:33:59.370
And he opens it, he takes out a burrito, and then he walks into the annex.
他打开微波炉，拿出一个卷饼，然后走进了分部办公室。

813
00:34:00.010 --> 00:34:04.510
And then there's the scene with Pam and Phyllis noticing that they have the same outfit on.
接着就是帕姆和菲利斯发现她们穿了同款衣服的那场戏。

814
00:34:05.070 --> 00:34:12.350
After the scene is over, and Phyllis has said her famous line, Aaron walks into the kitchen, checks the microwave,
在这场戏结束、菲利斯说了那句名言之后，阿伦走进茶水间，检查微波炉，

815
00:34:12.630 --> 00:34:15.870
and she's really confused, and she turns to Pam, and she says,
她感到非常困惑，转头对帕姆说：

816
00:34:15.990 --> 00:34:18.390
Did you see me put a burrito in there?
“你看到我把卷饼放进去了吗？”

817
00:34:19.430 --> 00:34:20.910
Because her burrito is missing.
因为她的卷饼不见了。

818
00:34:20.910 --> 00:34:25.930
And I just think it's such a great example of the kind of things that we had to lose
我只是觉得这真是一个很好的例子，说明了为了让这些剧集的电视播出版符合时长限制，

819
00:34:26.510 --> 00:34:30.630
in order to make the broadcast version of these episodes fit for time.
我们不得不剪掉哪些内容。

820
00:34:31.030 --> 00:34:36.970
These Superfan episodes, like, you're able to fill out the world with, like, mundane office life like this,
这些超级粉丝版，能让你通过诸如办公室里的日常琐事来丰满整个世界，

821
00:34:37.090 --> 00:34:39.170
like getting your burrito stolen out of the microwave.
比如你在微波炉里的卷饼被偷了。

822
00:34:40.210 --> 00:34:45.870
And for the most part, the extra stuff in the Superfan of Casual Friday are just those little scene extensions,
总的来说，《随性星期五》超级粉丝版中多出来的内容只是那些小小的场景延伸，

823
00:34:45.870 --> 00:34:47.110
and they're really fun.
而且真的很有趣。

824
00:34:47.570 --> 00:34:48.490
I just love it.
我太喜欢了。

825
00:34:48.490 --> 00:34:54.450
I love that burrito moment, made it back in, and Dave Rogers, thank you.
我很高兴那个卷饼的桥段能重新剪辑进去，谢谢你，戴夫·罗杰斯。

826
00:34:54.710 --> 00:34:59.330
Well, listen, next up, Dwight is going to gather everyone down in the warehouse to make his case.
好啦，听着，接下来，德怀特要把大家召集到仓库里来为自己辩护。

827
00:34:59.490 --> 00:35:07.170
Remember, he's written a memo to the sales staff in Invisible Ink that is actually urine.
记住，他给销售人员写了一份隐形墨水备忘录，那其实是尿液。

828
00:35:07.670 --> 00:35:14.070
And they are mad because Michael has come back, and he has made Pam and Brian salespeople.
他们很生气，因为迈克尔回来了，而且他把帕姆和布莱恩任命为了销售人员。

829
00:35:14.070 --> 00:35:21.090
And they're not giving back the clients that they stole when they left to make Michael Scott Paper Company.
他们不肯归还在离开去创立“迈克尔·斯科特纸业公司”时抢走的客户。

830
00:35:21.270 --> 00:35:22.470
So everyone's really mad.
所以每个人都非常生气。

831
00:35:22.970 --> 00:35:28.870
So Dwight calls this meeting, and he is down there with Phyllis, Stanley, and Andy.
于是德怀特召开了这次会议，他和菲利斯、斯坦利以及安迪一起在仓库里。

832
00:35:29.170 --> 00:35:32.630
And this is extended in the Superfan version.
这部分在超级粉丝版中进行了扩充。

833
00:35:33.350 --> 00:35:36.610
Dwight is explaining that failure is not an option.
德怀特在解释“失败不是选项”。

834
00:35:36.610 --> 00:35:37.510
Have a listen.
听听看。

835
00:35:38.230 --> 00:35:40.990
If we do nothing, we fail, and failure is not an option.
如果我们什么都不做，我们就会失败，而失败不是选项。

836
00:35:41.350 --> 00:35:43.410
Well, to be clear, it is an option.
好吧，明确一下，这确实是个选项。

837
00:35:43.650 --> 00:35:44.430
Not in my book.
在我看来不是。

838
00:35:45.010 --> 00:35:47.350
My book, the cover, is failure is not an option.
我的书，封面上就写着“失败不是选项”。

839
00:35:47.550 --> 00:35:48.650
It is an option.
它就是一个选项。

840
00:35:48.830 --> 00:35:49.590
Not in my book.
在我看来不是。

841
00:35:50.250 --> 00:35:50.670
Literally.
字面意思。

842
00:35:51.130 --> 00:35:51.190
What book?
什么书？

843
00:35:51.470 --> 00:35:51.890
What are you doing?
你在干什么？

844
00:35:51.930 --> 00:35:52.770
Did you write it?
是你写的吗？

845
00:35:53.170 --> 00:35:53.450
Yeah.
对。

846
00:35:54.150 --> 00:35:55.330
Failure is not an option.
《失败不是选项》。

847
00:35:55.550 --> 00:35:56.350
Very serious.
非常严肃。

848
00:35:57.130 --> 00:36:00.610
I got curious about the phrase, failure is not an option.
我对“失败不是选项”这个短语很好奇。

849
00:36:00.850 --> 00:36:02.470
I was like, where did that come from?
我在想，这是从哪来的？

850
00:36:03.150 --> 00:36:04.370
What did you find?
你发现了什么？

851
00:36:05.090 --> 00:36:08.650
I was completely surprised by the answer.
我对这个答案感到非常意外。

852
00:36:08.810 --> 00:36:10.330
Where do you guys think it came from?
你们觉得这句话是哪来的？

853
00:36:10.470 --> 00:36:14.370
Matt, Angela, if you had to guess, the phrase, failure is not an option.
马特、安吉拉，如果让你们猜的话，“失败不是选项”这句话。

854
00:36:14.490 --> 00:36:15.150
Unless you know.
除非你们本来就知道。

855
00:36:15.230 --> 00:36:15.810
Maybe you know.
也许你们知道。

856
00:36:15.890 --> 00:36:17.430
It sounds like a military term.
听起来像是个军事术语。

857
00:36:17.850 --> 00:36:18.850
Yeah, that's what I was going to say.
对，我刚正想这么说。

858
00:36:19.010 --> 00:36:21.250
I was like, oh, this is Winston Churchill.
我还以为，哦，这是温斯顿·丘吉尔说的。

859
00:36:22.170 --> 00:36:25.030
No, it came from the movie Apollo 13.
不，它出自电影《阿波罗13号》。

860
00:36:25.030 --> 00:36:29.590
Not the actual mission by the astronauts.
不是宇航员们的实际任务。

861
00:36:29.830 --> 00:36:29.930
Okay.
好的。

862
00:36:30.090 --> 00:36:30.310
Correct.
正确。

863
00:36:30.630 --> 00:36:31.390
So, sort of.
所以，算是有吧。

864
00:36:31.610 --> 00:36:32.710
I mean, influenced by.
我的意思是，受其影响。

865
00:36:32.890 --> 00:36:39.210
So, according to Wikipedia, in preparation for the movie, the script writers, Al Reinhart
根据维基百科，在筹备这部电影时，编剧阿尔·莱恩哈特

866
00:36:39.210 --> 00:36:43.970
and Bill Broyles, they interviewed flight controller Jerry Bostic.
和比尔·布罗伊尔斯采访了飞行控制员杰瑞·博斯蒂克。

867
00:36:44.250 --> 00:36:47.890
They wanted to get some intel on like, what is mission control really like?
他们想打听一下，任务控制中心到底是什么样的？

868
00:36:48.110 --> 00:36:54.710
And one of the questions they asked him was, weren't there times when everybody or even
他们问的问题之一是，难道没有过那种所有人甚至

869
00:36:54.710 --> 00:36:57.050
just a few people were completely panicked?
哪怕只有几个人彻底陷入恐慌的时候吗？

870
00:36:58.590 --> 00:37:00.850
And Jerry said, no.
杰瑞说，没有。

871
00:37:01.430 --> 00:37:07.150
When bad things happened, we just calmly laid out all the options and failure was not
当糟糕的事情发生时，我们只是冷静地列出所有的备选方案，而失败不在

872
00:37:07.150 --> 00:37:07.690
one of them.
选项之内。

873
00:37:08.550 --> 00:37:10.110
That was what he said to them.
这就是他对他们说的话。

874
00:37:11.170 --> 00:37:16.350
And then this guy, Jerry, said months later, he learned that when the writers got in their
后来这个叫杰瑞的家伙说，几个月后他得知，编剧们上

875
00:37:16.350 --> 00:37:19.550
car to leave, the writers said, that's it.
车离开时，编剧们说，就是它了。

876
00:37:19.690 --> 00:37:22.130
That's the tagline for this whole movie.
这就是整部电影的宣传标语。

877
00:37:22.570 --> 00:37:24.710
Failure is not an option.
失败不是选项。

878
00:37:24.950 --> 00:37:30.430
And then they gave that line to Ed Harris, who played mission control officer Gene Kranz.
然后他们把这句台词给了饰演任务控制官吉恩·克兰兹的埃德·哈里斯。

879
00:37:30.430 --> 00:37:36.830
And then later, Gene Kranz wrote a memoir titled, Failure is Not an Option.
再后来，吉恩·克兰兹写了一本自传，书名就叫《失败不是选项》。

880
00:37:37.210 --> 00:37:40.550
This is life imitating art, art imitating life.
这就是生活模仿艺术，艺术模仿生活。

881
00:37:40.770 --> 00:37:44.470
Before 1995, were people not really saying failure is not an option?
在1995年之前，人们难道真的不说“失败不是选项”吗？

882
00:37:44.750 --> 00:37:47.010
I mean, I really deep dived it.
我是说，我真的深入研究过。

883
00:37:47.230 --> 00:37:49.110
I don't recall saying it before then.
我不记得在那之前听人说过。

884
00:37:49.250 --> 00:37:50.250
Isn't that crazy?
这难道不疯狂吗？

885
00:37:50.430 --> 00:37:54.410
That's what surprised me because I felt like that's as old as it is.
这让我感到意外，因为我感觉这句话历史悠久。

886
00:37:54.610 --> 00:37:57.170
That's as far back in history as that phrase goes.
这句话在历史上的追溯也就到此为止了。

887
00:37:57.170 --> 00:38:02.090
But what was also crazy is that Gene Kranz never said it.
但同样疯狂的是，吉恩·克兰兹本人从未说过这句话。

888
00:38:02.330 --> 00:38:07.710
He never actually said that phrase, but his character in the movie said it.
他实际上从未说过这句话，但他在电影里的角色说了。

889
00:38:07.930 --> 00:38:11.070
But that was like the overall vibe of mission control.
不过那正是任务控制中心整体的氛围。

890
00:38:11.530 --> 00:38:12.830
I mean, it's good.
我是说，这很好。

891
00:38:13.290 --> 00:38:14.430
It's concise.
很简练。

892
00:38:14.770 --> 00:38:15.510
You get it.
你一听就懂。

893
00:38:15.670 --> 00:38:16.930
Failure is not an option, period.
失败不是选项，就这么简单。

894
00:38:17.530 --> 00:38:17.750
Yeah.
对。

895
00:38:18.050 --> 00:38:18.770
It's very direct.
非常直接。

896
00:38:19.070 --> 00:38:20.690
What a star-studded cast, by the way.
顺便说一句，这演员阵容真是群星璀璨。

897
00:38:20.830 --> 00:38:25.550
Oh, if you haven't watched Apollo 13 in a while, I'd like to say that the movie holds up.
哦，如果你有一阵子没看《阿波罗13号》了，我想说这部电影经得起时间考验。

898
00:38:25.670 --> 00:38:26.430
I watched it recently.
我最近刚看过。

899
00:38:26.430 --> 00:38:27.370
Yeah, it's been a while.
对，已经过去挺久了。

900
00:38:27.630 --> 00:38:28.290
It's great.
太棒了。

901
00:38:28.890 --> 00:38:29.430
All right.
好的。

902
00:38:29.650 --> 00:38:31.710
Well, listen, back to this scene.
听着，回到这场戏。

903
00:38:31.710 --> 00:38:33.590
I do want to bring up one other thing.
我还想提出另一件事。

904
00:38:33.870 --> 00:38:38.710
Jim is going to tell Pam, Michael, and Ryan that, quote, there may or may not be, but definitely
吉姆要告诉帕姆、迈克尔和瑞安，引用原话，仓库里可能，或者说并不一定，但绝对

905
00:38:38.710 --> 00:38:41.890
is, a mutiny forming in the warehouse right now.
是，现在正在酝酿一场哗变。

906
00:38:42.450 --> 00:38:45.010
And I have some candy bag alts for you, lady.
我这里还有一些糖果袋备选台词，女士。

907
00:38:45.770 --> 00:38:46.010
Okay.
好的。

908
00:38:46.530 --> 00:38:49.210
Michael is ticked off, and he has this talking head.
迈克尔生气了，他有这样一个单人访谈镜头。

909
00:38:49.370 --> 00:38:52.390
I want to play what made it in the episode, and then I'm going to read some alts.
我想播放正片里剪进去的内容，然后我再读一些备选台词。

910
00:38:52.550 --> 00:38:53.130
Okay, great.
好的，太棒了。

911
00:38:54.010 --> 00:38:58.130
The old Michael Scott might have taken this, but not the new Michael Scott.
过去的迈克尔·斯科特可能会忍气吞声，但现在的迈克尔·斯科特可不会。

912
00:38:58.590 --> 00:39:01.590
They are in for a bitter surprise.
他们要大吃一惊了。

913
00:39:01.590 --> 00:39:03.550
I am not to be truffled with.
我可不是好惹的。

914
00:39:04.170 --> 00:39:05.870
He's not to be truffled with.
他可不是好惹的。

915
00:39:05.890 --> 00:39:06.370
He's not.
他确实不是。

916
00:39:06.370 --> 00:39:08.130
No, don't truffle with him.
不，别去惹他。

917
00:39:08.250 --> 00:39:09.270
Don't truffle with him.
别去惹他。

918
00:39:09.590 --> 00:39:12.970
Don't even go near his trials and tribionis, okay?
连他的艰难险阻都别靠近，好吗？

919
00:39:12.970 --> 00:39:13.510
That's right.
没错。

920
00:39:13.810 --> 00:39:17.530
But here were some candy bag alts for that particular talking head.
但针对那个特定的访谈，还有一些糖果袋备选台词。

921
00:39:17.750 --> 00:39:24.170
Michael would have said, in my house, in my house, in my house, in my house.
迈克尔会说，在我地盘上，在我地盘上，在我地盘上，在我地盘上。

922
00:39:25.310 --> 00:39:27.110
He just would have said that over and over.
他就会一遍又一遍地这么说。

923
00:39:27.510 --> 00:39:28.430
Here's another one.
这是另一个。

924
00:39:28.970 --> 00:39:35.010
When you owe me an apology and instead give me a mutiny, you are asking for a smackdown.
当你欠我一个道歉却反而搞起哗变时，你就是在自讨苦吃。

925
00:39:37.780 --> 00:39:38.600
What's that?
那是什么？

926
00:39:39.260 --> 00:39:40.760
Smackdown truck backing up.
教训大卡车正倒车开过来。

927
00:39:40.880 --> 00:39:42.900
We've got a shipment of smackdown.
我们有一批教训到货了。

928
00:39:43.140 --> 00:39:44.300
Where would you like it?
你想卸在哪？

929
00:39:44.460 --> 00:39:45.200
Right here.
就这儿。

930
00:39:45.420 --> 00:39:46.660
You need to sign for it.
你需要签收一下。

931
00:39:47.140 --> 00:39:47.620
Gladly.
乐意之至。

932
00:39:48.060 --> 00:39:52.940
Oh, those are some of my favorite Michael talking heads, and they're my favorite ones
哦，这些是我最喜欢的迈克尔访谈之一，也是我最喜欢的

933
00:39:52.940 --> 00:39:56.460
that Steve does because he nails that timing so great.
史蒂夫的表现，因为他把那个时机掌握得太棒了。

934
00:39:57.220 --> 00:40:02.280
Also, this is bringing up an aspect of this episode that I really, really liked, which
另外，这也让我想起了这一集里我非常非常喜欢的一个方面，那就是

935
00:40:02.280 --> 00:40:08.200
is the whole thing for Michael in this episode is he's waiting all day for people to apologize
迈克尔在这一集里的整条主线就是他整天都在等着别人向他

936
00:40:08.200 --> 00:40:08.860
to him.
道歉。

937
00:40:09.060 --> 00:40:15.400
Like, his come from is that he is owed an apology, and I love it so much.
就好像，他的出发点就是别人欠他一个道歉，我太喜欢这个设定了。

938
00:40:15.400 --> 00:40:18.780
It's one of my favorite, like, mini storylines within this episode.
这是这一集里我最喜欢的迷你剧情之一。

939
00:40:19.120 --> 00:40:23.740
I really wish we could have heard Steve say, we've got a shipment of smackdown.
我真希望我们能听到史蒂夫说，我们有一批教训到货了。

940
00:40:24.000 --> 00:40:24.600
I know.
我知道。

941
00:40:25.400 --> 00:40:26.800
All right, here's another one.
